"Grave_Circle_A": {"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/NAMA_Gold_diadem_with_repouss%C3%A9_rosettes_and_an_infant%2C_consisting_of_pieces_of_gold_foil-_Grave_Circle_A.JPG/1920px-NAMA_Gold_diadem_with_repouss%C3%A9_rosettes_and_an_infant%2C_consisting_of_pieces_of_gold_foil-_Grave_Circle_A.JPG","title":"Grave Circle A","desc":"An impressive gold diadem with repoussé rosettes and thin sheets applied at the top. Grave Circle A, Mycenae,16th century BCE. A unique gold covering for the body and the face of an infant, consisting of pieces of gold foil. A distinctive detail are the ring-shaped earrings. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NAMA_Gold_diadem_with_repouss%C3%A9_rosettes_and_an_infant,_consisting_of_pieces_of_gold_foil-_Grave_Circle_A.JPG","alt":"NAMA Gold diadem with repoussé rosettes and an infant, consisting of pieces of gold foil- Grave Circle A"},
